{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 49,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah. Hear this, all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " people; give ear, all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " inhabitants of the world:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Both low and high, rich and poor together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will incline my ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why should I fear in the days of evil, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the iniquity of my heels shall encompass me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "None ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For the redemption of their soul ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " precious, and it ceaseth for ever:)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That he should still live for ever, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not see corruption.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he seeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their inward thought ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their houses ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall continue",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for ever, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their dwelling places to all generations; they call ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lands after their own names.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in honor abideth not: he is like the beasts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This their way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.49.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.49.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in honor, and understandeth not, is like the beasts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
